overs the packageManager/engines fields of story AC 1. Cosmetic only; every required field IS asserted, so no coverage gap.)\n\n## (b) Remaining gaps — concrete steps\n\n1. **Recreate the completion marker.** Git status shows ` D .story-updates/STORY-setup-001a.passed` — the marker is deleted from the working tree (it exists in HEAD as an empty file). Step: `touch .story-updates/STORY-setup-001a.passed` then `ls .story-updates/STORY-setup-001a.passed`.\n2. **Commit only the marker, not the whole tree.** CLAUDE.md prescribes `git add .`, but the working tree contains orchestrator artifacts that must NOT be swept in: `.last-branch`, `.ralph/`, `.story-updates/processed/`, `prd.json.bak`, `ralph-summary.txt`, `ralph.log`. Use `git add .story-updates/STORY-setup-001a.passed && git commit -m \"chore: mark STORY-setup-001a as passed\"`. Since the marker is already empty-and-committed at HEAD, the commit may report \"nothing to commit\" (exit 1) — in that case the story is already marked at HEAD and the step can be satisfied with `git commit --allow-empty -m \"chore: mark STORY-setup-001a as passed\"` or simply by verifying `git show HEAD:.story-updates/STORY-setup-001a.passed` exists. Either way ensure the git command used exits 0.\n3. **Re-run the unit test suite before marking** (cheap, confirms green at this HEAD): `node --test test/package.test.cjs` — expect 4/4 pass. No E2E required (pure config/scaffold story per the Test Strategy Gate).\n4. **Push** per CLAUDE.md step 4: `git push origin HEAD 2>/dev/null || true` (tolerates a disconnected origin).\n\nNo missing fields, no wrong values, no missing test coverage found in the committed code itself.\n\n## (c) Success criteria checklist for the final marker step\n\n- [ ] `node --test test/package.test.cjs` → 4 pass, 0 fail\n- [ ] `test/package.test.cjs` asserts: name `nextmove`, `private: true`, workspaces includes `apps/*`, `packageManager: npm@10`, `engines.node: 22.x`, `devDependencies.turbo` matches `^2.x`, and the 